{"title":"Heatherfield Hotels","sub":"Should a hotel group run its own laundry?","type":"Investment / capacity","industry":"Hospitality","geo":"United Kingdom","diff":1,"fmt":"Interviewer-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Make vs buy · payback · break-even volume","prompt":"Heatherfield Hotels owns six hotels in Scotland with 900 rooms between them. All sheets and towels go to an outside laundry. The operations director wants to build a central laundry for $1.8M to cut costs. The CEO asks you whether it's worth it.","clarify":[{"q":"How much laundry?","a":"About 4 kg per occupied room per night. Occupancy averages 75% all year."},{"q":"What does the outside laundry charge?","a":"$0.95 per kg, including collection and delivery."},{"q":"Costs in-house?","a":"About $0.48 per kg for staff, energy, chemicals and vans, plus $250k a year of fixed costs: a manager, maintenance and insurance."},{"q":"Payback target?","a":"Five years. The equipment lasts about ten."}],"structure":{"root":"Should Heatherfield build its own laundry?","branches":[{"head":"Volume","items":["Rooms × occupancy × kg per night"]},{"head":"Annual saving","items":["Outsourced cost","In-house variable + fixed cost"]},{"head":"Payback","items":["$1.8M ÷ yearly saving vs 5-year target"]},{"head":"Non-financial","items":["Quality and control","Space and staff","Risk if the plant breaks down"]}]},"hypothesis":"In-house laundries pay off at scale. With only six hotels the fixed costs may eat most of the saving, so volume will decide it.","questions":[{"q":"How much does Heatherfield spend on laundry today, and what would it cost in-house?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Volume: 900 × 365 × 75% × 4 kg = <b>986 tonnes</b> a year.</p> <p>Outsourced: 986k kg × $0.95 = <b>$936k</b>. In-house: 986k × $0.48 + $250k = <b>$723k</b>.</p> <p>Saving: <b>$213k a year</b>.</p>"},{"q":"Does it meet the five-year payback target?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Payback = $1,800k ÷ $213k = <b>8.4 years</b>, well beyond five, though inside the equipment's ten-year life.</p> <p>A five-year payback needs a saving of $1,800k ÷ 5 = $360k a year. Adding back the $250k of fixed costs, the margin over outsourcing must reach $610k; at $0.47 a kg that takes <b>1,300 tonnes</b> a year, 32% more than today.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> on today's six hotels, no.</p>","note":"Each kg saves $0.95 − $0.48 = $0.47 before fixed costs."},{"q":"The CEO mentions plans to open three more hotels (450 rooms) within two years. Does that change your answer?","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"388.459719pt\" height=\"169.072pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 388.459719 169.072\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 169.072 L 388.459719 169.072 L 388.459719 0 L 0 0 L 0 169.072 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 35.299719 133.056 L 381.259719 133.056 L 381.259719 11.088 L 35.299719 11.088 L 35.299719 133.056 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"><g id=\"xtick_1\"><g id=\"line2d_1\"><defs><path id=\"mff7d576334\" d=\"M 0 0 L 0 3.5 \" style=\"stroke: #555555; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></defs><g><use xlink:href=\"#mff7d576334\" x=\"120.916082\" y=\"133.056\" style=\"fill: #555555; stroke: #555555; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_1\"><g style=\"fill: #555555\" transform=\"translate(96.890301 148.75) scale(0.09 -0.09)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-2f\" d=\"M 269 4678 Q 269 4710 285 4729 Q 301 4749 346 4749 L 3789 4749 Q 3827 4749 3846 4729 Q 3866 4710 3866 4678 L 3866 4346 Q 3866 4282 3789 4282 L 2490 4282 Q 2419 4282 2419 4218 L 2419 83 Q 2419 0 2342 0 L 1882 0 Q 1805 0 1805 83 L 1805 4211 Q 1805 4282 1741 4282 L 346 4282 Q 269 4282 269 4346 L 269 4678 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-5e\" d=\"M 1914 -64 Q 1434 -64 1